Make kChromeAppsEnabled exist on Android.

Replaces Kiwi's version, which appended `|| true` to the platform condition:

    -#if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
    -    BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
    +    BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA) || true

Same objection as 0001: it makes the guard unconditional rather than saying
which platform it is for, so the condition no longer documents anything and any
platform upstream adds silently inherits it.

The pref itself is needed because Cobalt supports extensions on Android, and the
code paths that read kChromeAppsEnabled are compiled in as a result. Without the
symbol they fail to link.

--- a/extensions/browser/pref_names.cc
+++ b/extensions/browser/pref_names.cc
@@
 const char kDeletedComponentExtensions[] =
     "extensions.deleted_component_extensions";
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN) || BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC) || BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || \
-    BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
+    BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA) || BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 extern const char kChromeAppsEnabled[] = "extensions.chrome_apps_enabled";
 #endif
